Probably the easiest role to start with is Knight.  You start with
half-decent armor, the ability to ride and joust, and have a long sword
just begging to be dipped into a fountain (over and over, if necessary) to
acquire Excalibur.  While not the most damaging of weapons, it provides
level drain resistance and automatic searching.

The most difficult thing as a Knight I found was to keep my horse from
starving.  If you can find a scroll of taming or two, a dragon makes a
much superior steed (black dragons can't be disintegrated from under you,
and yellow dragons can't be stoned - the rest aren't of any particularly
special value).

It's also a good idea to remember some of the role-specific alignment
penalties that can be incurred.  Knights can't attack a fleeing monster
without losing alignment ("You caitiff!"), for example.

But overall, don't attack what you can't kill, and don't go deeper than
your level until you're well equipped (though I've been killed killed
several times as level 7 or so on dungeon level 4 by soldier ants, which
are often generated too soon, in my opinion).


